<!--
  PLAYER swipe indicator, active page.

  The frozen `swipe` row is three 10x10 slots edge to edge, and the active one is
  not a dot:

    `swipe > Shape Set`   INSTANCE, variant Shape = "9-sided cookie"
    `Shape Set > shape`   VECTOR 8.53 x 8.42 at (0.74, 0.79) of the 10x10 slot

  So the active marker is a nine-lobed scalloped disc, 8.53 x 8.42 centred in its
  slot - (0.74 + 8.53/2, 0.79 + 8.42/2) is (5.0, 5.0). The inactive ones are plain
  circles, 8.42 across. The app drew three identical white ovals filling the whole
  10dp before this.

  The exporter records a vector's box but never its geometry, so the outline here
  is derived rather than copied. The derivation is the box:

    r(t) = 1 + a * cos(9 * (t + pi/2))

  a nine-fold scalloped disc with one lobe pointing up. Its bounding box is only
  square when a = 0; the frozen 8.53 x 8.42 fixes the ratio at 1.01306, and
  a = 0.081 reproduces that to six decimal places. Sampled as 27 cubics - three
  per lobe, which holds the analytic curve to 0.014dp - and scaled so the path's
  own bounds are exactly the frozen 8.53 x 8.42.

  Control points sit slightly outside the viewport at the extremes; the curve
  itself does not.

  Untinted: `primary` at full opacity, applied from the layout.
-->
